<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg wavelength at the 1.178 mm shell-thickness tier of Aptenodytes forsteri (Aptenodytes forsteri (Emperor penguin), Holocene, 0 Ma)",
        "Schnakenberg wavelength at the 1.178 mm shell-thickness tier of Aptenodytes forsteri faithfully reproduces Aptenodytes forsteri (Emperor penguin), Holocene, 0 Ma morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Aptenodytes forsteri (Emperor penguin), Holocene, 0 Ma specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Aptenodytes forsteri (Emperor penguin), Holocene, 0 Ma" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim a predecessor chronospecies; the series length is 1.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim body-scale black-white countershading is a 1.178 mm Turing mode.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the MHNT photograph's 0.66 mm pore FFT equals lambda_c.",
        "does_not_claim: Sibling slot 119 parameters (alpha 1.31) are not used.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Commensurate-scale sweep comparing dispersion wavelength to the PDE Fourier peak.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Median-to-99.5th-percentile display of the activator so one hot pixel cannot hide the lattice.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics a=0.20, b=0.30, D_v/D_u=42, with D_u set so the fastest mode is 10^(-2.929) m.",
        "reported_in_source: Chinese Journal of Polar Research 2008: emperor egg 121.3 by 83.8 mm, shell thickness 1.11 mm (0.94-1.32).",
        "reported_in_source: Prum and Williamson 2002: within-feather pigment patterns can be RD spots, bars, and dot arrays.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation for a two-species reaction-diffusion system.",
        "transfer_boundary: Shell thickness is a through-shell length. Using it as the lateral wavelength is a scale identification for this tier, not a published pore-spacing measurement." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Aptenodytes forsteri" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Aves (Ornithes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Aptenodytes" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/aptenodytes_forsteri_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Aptenodytes forsteri (Emperor penguin), Holocene, 0 Ma; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Prum and Williamson 2002: within-feather pigment patterns can be RD spots, bars, and dot arrays. | Chinese Journal of Polar Research 2008: emperor egg 121.3 by 83.8 mm, shell thickness 1.11 mm (0.94-1.32).; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics a=0.20, b=0.30, D_v/D_u=42, with D_u set so the fastest mode is 10^(-2.929) m. | Commensurate-scale sweep comparing dispersion wavelength to the PDE Fourier peak. | Median-to-99.5th-percentile display of the activator so one hot pixel cannot hide the lattice.; transfer_boundary: Shell thickness is a through-shell length. Using it as the lateral wavelength is a scale identification for this tier, not a published pore-spacing measurement.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the MHNT photograph's 0.66 mm pore FFT equals lambda_c. | Does not claim body-scale black-white countershading is a 1.178 mm Turing mode. | Does not claim a predecessor chronospecies; the series length is 1. | Sibling slot 119 parameters (alpha 1.31) are not used.]; other sources: Eco-biology of eggs of emperor penguin and its comparison with other sea bird eggs in Antarctica <https://journal.chinare.org.cn/EN/Y2008/V20/I4/320>, Egg of Aptenodytes forsteri, Muséum de Toulouse <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aptenodytes_forsteri_MHNT.jpg>; phenomenon_size: 920 µm (0.00092 m, log10=-3.036 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 920 µm to 2.65 m): 920 µm:aptenodytes-forsteri-bioelectric-polarity, 3.3 mm:aptenodytes-forsteri-vertex-packing, 5.9 cm:aptenodytes-forsteri-turing-wavelength, 11.1 cm:aptenodytes-